      "object_role": "interpretation",
      "proposed_content": "The prose-secure mechanism converts mean-square control into an almost-everywhere statement with finite logarithmic exceptional measure. Low zeros are bounded separately; the high-zero tail is controlled in L2 on each multiplicative interval, which bounds that interval's bad set, and geometric scale selection makes the bad-set measures summable.",
